# Cozy - a zsh prompt

This is a zsh prompt made from scratch only utilizing native zsh functionality
no frameworks or anything. It aims to be understated and subtle. It uses
vertical features on the left and right to visually tie prompt and command
line(s) together and contrast them with all the other lines, the output from
all the programs.


## Prerequisits

This prompt is designed for a solarized-dark colortheme. It works best if the
colortheme has default background set to base03. The file
Solarized_Dark_anygard is a [ghostty|https://ghostty.org/] theme file for such
a theme.


## Customization

There is support for the following zstyle contexts and styles

### :cozy:background regular

Set the color of the regular prompt background. Takes an integer in the 0-15
range the value is the color index in a 16 color theme. 


### :cozy:foreground regular

Set the color of the regular prompt foreground. Takes an integer in the 0-15
range the value is the color index in a 16 color theme. 


### :cozy:foreground warning

Set the color of the foreground of warning messages. Takes an integer in the 0-15
range the value is the color index in a 16 color theme. 


### :cozy:foreground error

Set the color of the foreground of error messages. Takes an integer in the 0-15
range the value is the color index in a 16 color theme. 

### :cozy:foreground primary_accent

Set the color of the foreground of text with the primary accent. Takes an
integer in the 0-15 range the value is the color index in a 16 color theme. 


### :cozy:foreground secondary_accent

Set the color of the foreground of text with the secondary accent. Takes an
integer in the 0-15 range the value is the color index in a 16 color theme. 


### :cozy:vcs:char banner

Set the banner character for VCS info in the prompt. Takes a character value
either as a character or in unicode $'\XXXX' notation.


### :cozy:vcs:char staged

Set the staged character for VCS info in the prompt. Takes a character value
either as a character or in unicode $'\XXXX' notation.


### :cozy:vcs:char unstaged

Set the unstaged character for VCS info in the prompt. Takes a character value
either as a character or in unicode $'\XXXX' notation.


### :cozy:marker left

Set the character written in the very first position on all lines associated
with the prompt. Takes a character value either as a character or in unicode
$'\XXXX' notation.


### :cozy:marker right

Set the character written in the very last position on all lines associated
with the prompt. Takes a character value either as a character or in unicode
$'\XXXX' notation.
